* TR-1um IP62 RF varactor overlay -- MOS and junction varactors.
*
* The baseline model files are NOT modified.  This file provides four
* two/three-terminal varactor wrappers built on the existing devices.
*
* =====================================================================
* 1. MOS varactors (recommended; uses the existing BSIM3 C-V, capmod=2)
* =====================================================================
*   NMOS_var  : VSS-referenced.  D/S/B are tied to `minus`; the gate is
*               `plus`.  The body is the p-substrate, so no isolation is
*               needed and LVS is clean.
*   PMOS_var  : VDD-referenced.  D/S are tied to `minus`; the gate is `plus`;
*               the n-well body is the separate `bw` terminal (tie to VDD).
*               `bw` is exposed because connect_global(WN,"VDD") fixes the
*               well potential in layout.
*
*   Both are multi-finger (nf) to reduce the gate resistance.  The C-V curve
*   is the BSIM3 capmod=2 result; no new fitting is claimed.  Expect a
*   practical Cmax/Cmin of 2-3, not the ideal 7-9, and Q limited by Rg and
*   the well/channel resistance.
*
*   Bias range: keep |Vgs| <= 5 V.  NMOS_var tunes for Vg > Vth; PMOS_var
*   tunes for Vg < VDD - |Vth|.
*
* =====================================================================
* 2. Junction varactors (engineering abrupt-junction first pass)
* =====================================================================
*   DP_var : p+ / n-well, anode=`plus`, cathode=`minus`.
*   DN_var : n+ / p-sub,  anode=`minus`, cathode=`plus` (see note below).
*
*   The baseline DP/DN models carry only is/rs/cj/cjsw/bv and NO grading
*   coefficient or built-in potential, so their C(V) shape is undefined.
*   These wrappers add the missing terms with an ENGINEERING ABRUPT-JUNCTION
*   assumption:
*       mj = 0.5   (abrupt junction)
*       pb = 0.9 V (built-in potential)
*       cj = 1.02 fF/um^2 (DP, p+/n-well) / 0.744 fF/um^2 (DN, n+/p-sub)
*            taken from the baseline MOS junction values
*       cjsw = 0.2 fF/um
*   The area is given in um^2 via `a`; the perimeter is the equivalent square.
*   This is a first-order model: replace mj/pb/cj with measured C-V data
*   before using it for a tuned tank.
*
*   DN_var is drawn as n+ in p-sub.  In this PDK the substrate is the global
*   VSS, so DN_var's cathode (`plus`) is the p-substrate: it is a VSS-referenced
*   device and cannot float.
*
* Usage:
*   XV1 gate 0       NMOS_var w=40u l=1u nf=8
*   XV2 gate 0 vdd   PMOS_var w=40u l=1u nf=8
*   XD1 anode 0      DP_var a=100
*   XD2 0 cathode    DN_var a=100

* ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
* MOS varactors
* ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
.subckt NMOS_var plus minus
.param w=10u l=1u nf=1 rshg=95
Xcore minus plus minus minus NMOS_nf w=w l=l nf=nf rshg=rshg
.ends NMOS_var

.subckt PMOS_var plus minus bw
.param w=20u l=1u nf=1 rshg=95
Xcore minus plus minus bw PMOS_nf w=w l=l nf=nf rshg=rshg
.ends PMOS_var

* ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
* Junction varactors -- engineering abrupt-junction models
* ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
.model DP_var_mst D tnom=27
+ is=2.457e-18 rs=0 cj=1.02e-3 mj=0.5 pb=0.9 cjsw=2.0e-10
+ bv=10.35 ibv=1.0e-6

.model DN_var_mst D tnom=27
+ is=1.0e-17 rs=0 cj=0.744e-3 mj=0.5 pb=0.9 cjsw=2.0e-10
+ bv=14.45 ibv=1.0e-6

.subckt DP_var plus minus
.param a=100 rs=33.71
D1 plus ni DP_var_mst area='a*1e-12' pj='4*sqrt(a)*1e-6'
Rser ni minus r='rs'
.ends DP_var

.subckt DN_var plus minus
.param a=100 rs=47.59
D1 minus ni DN_var_mst area='a*1e-12' pj='4*sqrt(a)*1e-6'
Rser ni plus r='rs'
.ends DN_var
